WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.990 align:start position:0%
 
one year ago  on this very day december 1st the  symptoms of the new coronavirus were  first detected in wuhan china  that's according to a published study  cbs news was the first u.s network to go  to wuhan before the city went into  lockdown in january i remember that  raymie andosencio just returned to show  us what life is like now  in the area where those first covet  cases were discovered  in this city of 11 million the world's  first epicenter of coronavirus  harsh lockdowns have given way to a  hardcore nightlife  at wuhan's central market a food vendor  tells us business is back and he's proud  and happy  that sense of optimism is shared by  students coming to see this massive new  government sanctioned exhibition  called people first lives first in the  same space as one of the earliest  biggest makeshift coveted hospitals it  hails  president xi jinping as heroic and the  strong leadership of china's communist  party  it also highlights frontline healthcare  workers but mentions of those who died  are hard to find attendees told us it  was factual  and comprehensive beijing having  declared victory in its war on kovid  has now opened new fronts trying to pin  its origin on other countries  including the u.s italy and india  although china was the first to report  cases  said foreign ministry spokesman jolie  jen just last week it doesn't  necessarily mean that the virus  originated in china  this is the wuhan institute of virology  believed by some to be the origin of  kovid 19. now we tried to get access to  this institute for months but we were  turned down  we also tried to interview many chinese  doctors across the country  they all said they were either busy or  were frankly barred from speaking with  us  we did speak with dr lin pha wong who's  been researching kovit's origin  what's the chance that the coronavirus  did not  originate in china origination is  difficult but let's face it a human  outbreak started in gohan  who works at a state-owned enterprise is  one of countless people still  looking for answers his father died from  kovid in february  the government sent condolences and  about 600 dollars as compensation  it felt hollow he said i still don't  know where the virus came from  if you ask me who to blame i don't know  and here we are again in wuhan outside  the city's first  hospital to receive coronavirus patients  dr wong says there are now  three major knowledge gaps we have to  fill in in order to beat this virus  one of course is covet's origin two is  why some patients take so long to  recover  and three how long antibodies can really  protect us  tony all right raymond asensio in wuhan  china for us remy thank you very much  he's been pioneering the coverage there  with the first network  and now he continues it those are other  big questions remaining though the ones  you pointed out at the end yeah  but we could learn so many lessons from  what they've been through i mean  what the experts agree on uniformly is  about mask  and everybody seems to have gotten that  message i think  except with the exception of the united  states we can and should do better i  like what they said  people people first lives first we are  unique and wonderful people  yes we are i love us  i love it i love us it's a great country  come visit sometimes sometimes we got  issues  i love us

